      "message": "I don\u0027t mind the extra name, but I think I would much prefer this to be\n\n`using SkFreeDeleter \u003d SkOverloadedFunctionObject\u003cvoid(void*), sk_free\u003e;`\n\nThough I realize this probably means splitting `SkOverloadedFunctionObject` and `SkFunctionObject` out of `SkTemplates.h` (or splitting everything else out of there) so that these can be included here. Then the `using` makes it obvious in the code that this is a convenience type, the `Overloaded` part makes it obvious in the code that we\u0027re doing this because we believe the function may be overloaded, and then the comment only needs to be \"OpenSSL declares a function which may be named sk_free.\"",
